    {
      "id": "noteIntro",
      "type": "NoteNode",
      "x": -40,
      "y": -243,
      "init": {
        "label": "Schedule",
        "body": "# When will it be done, and what can't slip?\nA **Schedule** node runs the critical-path method over a task list: each task's **Duration** in working days and the tasks it waits on (**Predecessors**).\n\nIt appends **Start · Finish · Float · Critical** to the rows. Float is how many days a task can slip without moving the finish; the tasks with none are the critical path. **Project finish** comes out as its own value, and **Gantt** is Mermaid source the Mermaid node draws.\n\nTry it: make Paint take 5 days instead of 2 and watch it join the critical path.",
        "color": "violet",
        "width": 380,
        "height": 270
      }
    },
    {
